{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-13T19:16:52.134Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"ea247dff672e9d17c830455f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"claim","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-13T19:16:52.134Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/assignee","value":"pi-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/claim_principal","value":"pi-agent"}],"before_hash":"52b9b4f7fe48859abeec401358858a4d683cd1e19f3b35e0ea4080b1e5040364","after_hash":"599e5294153fe5ca273bd7fb29b38d09890e52dea3c7f3177d8f24a7eacc58b8","item_hash_version":3,"message":"CodeRabbit round 2: fail closed on root-link and missing-registry findings","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d9f9a86e12d9b3571f1811fda283005693d5380a2b9fcbfefac23ed2204e4b44"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-13T19:17:15.434Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"ea247dff672e9d17c830455f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/12","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-13T19:17:15.434Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"CodeRabbit round 2 plan (two Major findings on collection): (1) root-path existence checks that use a link-following stat treat a dangling symlink as absence, so a broken oplog.jsonl, ref directory or lease directory silently loses its roots before a sweep. Fix: stat the three root paths without following links, refuse any non-ENOENT/broken entry with the existing unsafe_gc_roots errors, and keep true absence as absence. (2) the shared instance registry is read tolerantly, so a registry deleted after linking hides a live instance and an apply sweep can delete staged payloads reachable only through that instance's private index. Fix: initialization writes the canonical empty registry, and collection requires the registry to be present (fail closed) instead of treating absence as an empty registry. Both get real-repository regression tests plus behavioural revert proofs."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-13T19:17:15.434Z"}],"before_hash":"599e5294153fe5ca273bd7fb29b38d09890e52dea3c7f3177d8f24a7eacc58b8","after_hash":"ea7138b826e41692946238aa1dfe1b92072708122c22c9eabe41c14139953d5a","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"310e8cb4bf1903b3fdda414bb4195af431eec59826ee927d653a58a70eb9dad7"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-13T19:50:47.190Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"ea247dff672e9d17c830455f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/13","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-13T19:50:47.190Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Round 2 fixes implemented and proven. (1) Root-link strictness: collection now stats the oplog, ref and lease root paths without following links (true absence is ENOENT only, anything else refuses with the existing unsafe_gc_roots errors) in a requireEntry helper. Regression test 'dangling links at collection roots fail closed' covers all three roots and proves a real sweep still runs after the broken links are removed. Behavioural revert proof: reverting only the three requireEntry call sites to the link-following existence checks makes that test fail with 'Missing expected exception' — the dangling oplog is treated as an absent log and the sweep proceeds. (2) Registry fail-closed: repository initialization now writes the canonical empty instance registry, and collection requires the registry to be present instead of reading absence as empty. Regression test 'a hidden instance registry fails closed before any sweep can delete staged work' stages real work through a linked instance's private index and proves collection refuses (dry run and apply) once the registry is hidden, from both the hub and the instance, while the staged payload survives. Behavioural revert proof: reverting only the collection registry read to the tolerant empty-on-absent form makes that test fail with 'Missing expected exception' and would sweep the staged payload. Data-loss findings fail closed in both dry-run and apply. Full suite green."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-13T19:50:47.190Z"}],"before_hash":"ea7138b826e41692946238aa1dfe1b92072708122c22c9eabe41c14139953d5a","after_hash":"b91e2b429a20a050ff1c6a7902c6e0a7601ac7211c8bb42b38c2db8cced61646","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ec18e1d093a5581c022d165fc81c5260e7f40ee917423cf7c4d8e0835380b4bc"}
